<BaseLayout title="Privacy"><div class="page-wrap prose"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / PRE-LAUNCH DRAFT</span><h1>Your work deserves<br />a clear boundary.</h1><div class="notice">This implementation draft documents the intended data flows. The operator identity, contact details, deployment regions, processor terms, and final retention disclosures require review before public launch.</div><h2>Account information</h2><p>Accounts use Google sign-in or email/password through Supabase. Profile and device records support authentication, access management, and support. Never enter execution-provider API keys into this website.</p><h2>Usage reporting</h2><p>Reporting stores metadata: request IDs, provider/model, time, status, token usage, estimated model cost, routing reason, and timing. It does not store prompt text, responses, or code. Individual request details are retained for 30 days; daily aggregate totals for 12 months.</p><h2>Assessment context is separate</h2><p>The router may send compact current/recent conversation text to its selection backend and TypeSafe’s Jev API. Those excerpts may include private code or sensitive text. The current extraction logic does not automatically redact all secrets. Assessor retention and processor terms must be verified before production claims are made.</p><h2>Payments and emails</h2><p>Paddle is the selected merchant of record for paid subscriptions. Supabase and Resend support account emails. Payment card details belong in Paddle checkout, not Zusal analytics. Billing records may be retained separately from usage records where required.</p><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>The intended analytics are aggregate page visits, signups, and install-button clicks, without advertising trackers, prompts, or code. Collection defaults to disabled. When enabled after review, the endpoint counts events per page/day without visitor identifiers; signup submissions are approximate events, not verified unique accounts. Request transport still exposes an IP address to hosting providers, whose operational logging requires separate retention review. No third-party advertising scripts are included.</p><h2>Your controls</h2><p>Export available request history, revoke devices, or delete your account through Account Settings. Deletion requires recent authentication, stops access and future renewals, and removes profile/usage data. Separate billing retention and processor deletion responsibilities must be finalized.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Support is planned through the Discord community with private tickets for sensitive account concerns. The final legal contact and community invite are still to be configured.</p></div></BaseLayout>
